statement:
Let P ∈ ℕ, let μ be a measure on ℝ^P with support spt μ (Lean μ.support), and let S be a linear subspace of ℝ^P with orthogonal projection p_S (Lean S.starProjection). Let F ⊆ ℝ^P be a finite set, ξ, x₀ ∈ ℝ^P, and r, s, L ∈ ℝ. B̄_r(ξ) is the closed ball and ofReal = ENNReal.ofReal. Assume:
(i) for every x ∈ spt μ ∩ B̄_r(ξ) there is y ∈ F with dist(x, y) ≤ s;
(ii) |(y − x₀) − p_S(y − x₀)| ≤ L for every y ∈ F;
(iii) dist(x₀, ξ) ≤ s.
Then:
(a) |(x − ξ) − p_S(x − ξ)| ≤ 2s + L for every x ∈ spt μ ∩ B̄_r(ξ);
(b) ∫_{B̄_r(ξ)} ofReal(|(x − ξ) − p_S(x − ξ)|²) dμ(x) ≤ ofReal((2s + L)²)·μ(B̄_r(ξ)) in [0, ∞], where the integral is a lower Lebesgue integral.
